# ── Local Network / WiFi Demo Setup ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# To run a live demo where multiple laptops on the SAME WiFi network
# can all communicate in real time:
#
# 1. Find the host machine's local IP address:
#    - Windows: run `ipconfig` in terminal → look for "IPv4 Address" (e.g. 192.168.1.105)
#    - Mac/Linux: run `ifconfig` or `ip a` → look for inet (e.g. 192.168.1.105)
#
# 2. Replace 192.168.x.x below with that IP address.
#
# 3. Copy this file to `.env.local` (no ".example") in the frontend folder.
#
# 4. Start backend bound to all interfaces:
#    uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000
#    OR with Docker Compose: docker-compose up (already binds to 0.0.0.0)
#
# 5. Start frontend:
#    npm run dev
#
# 6. Each other laptop on the WiFi opens: http://192.168.x.x:3000/lobby
#    They can sign up, then create or join rooms using the invite code.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.x.x:8000
NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=ws://192.168.x.x:8000

# ── Demo User Accounts (pre-create these before the demo) ────────────────────
# Register 4 accounts at /signup, each with a different user_type:
#   - deaf@demo.com   → user_type: deaf   (sees captions + sign avatar)
#   - mute@demo.com   → user_type: mute   (types text, hears TTS voice)
#   - both@demo.com   → user_type: both   (all features enabled)
#   - norm@demo.com   → user_type: deaf   (speaks normally, gets transcribed)
#
# Demo flow:
#   1. deaf@demo.com creates a room → copies invite code
#   2. Others join with that code, each choosing their role
#   3. All 4 laptops open the chat room
#   4. Deaf user speaks → others see transcript + AI response
#   5. Mute user types → others see message + hear TTS
#   6. Sign avatar animates for all users when keywords are detected
